WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.472
<v Examiner>The male versus female table.

2
00:00:03.472 --> 00:00:04.183
<v Examiner>Six marks.

3
00:00:04.633 --> 00:00:09.892
<v Examiner>Tabulate the differences between the male and female reproductive systems, looking at:

4
00:00:09.892 --> 00:00:14.355
<v Examiner>the function of LH, the function of FSH, the timing of gamete production,

5
00:00:14.355 --> 00:00:19.247
<v Examiner>the size of the gametes, the timing of meiosis, and the mobility of the gametes.

6
00:00:19.697 --> 00:00:23.085
Six rows, two columns, and one line in each box.

7
00:00:23.085 --> 00:00:25.273
Every row has to be a contrast.

8
00:00:25.273 --> 00:00:29.297
A row with the same words in both columns scores nothing.

9
00:00:29.747 --> 00:00:30.627
Row one, LH.

10
00:00:30.627 --> 00:00:35.247
In females, it triggers ovulation, and forms the corpus luteum.

11
00:00:35.247 --> 00:00:39.795
In males, it stimulates the Leydig cells to make testosterone.

12
00:00:40.245 --> 00:00:41.201
Row two, FSH.

13
00:00:41.201 --> 00:00:44.659
In females, it stimulates follicle development.

14
00:00:44.659 --> 00:00:49.589
In males, it stimulates spermatogenesis, through the Sertoli cells.

15
00:00:50.039 --> 00:00:52.858
Row three, the timing of gamete production.

16
00:00:52.858 --> 00:00:57.579
Females start in fetal life, and release eggs from puberty to menopause.

17
00:00:57.579 --> 00:01:00.727
Males start at puberty, and keep going for life.

18
00:01:02.177 --> 00:01:03.191
Row four, size.

19
00:01:03.191 --> 00:01:07.180
The egg is the largest cell in the body, full of cytoplasm.

20
00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:10.155
The sperm is the smallest, with almost none.

21
00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:12.820
Row five, the timing of meiosis.

22
00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:17.250
In males it's continuous, and one spermatocyte gives four sperm.

23
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:23.134
In females it stops and starts, arresting in prophase one and again in metaphase two,

24
00:01:23.134 --> 00:01:26.456
and one oocyte gives one egg, plus polar bodies.

25
00:01:26.906 --> 00:01:28.160
Row six, mobility.

26
00:01:28.160 --> 00:01:30.946
Sperm are motile: they swim with a tail.

27
00:01:30.946 --> 00:01:32.757
The egg can't move itself.

28
00:01:32.757 --> 00:01:37.423
It's carried along the fallopian tube by cilia, and by peristalsis.

29
00:01:38.873 --> 00:01:39.571
The traps.

30
00:01:39.571 --> 00:01:43.685
LH in males goes to the Leydig cells, to make testosterone.

31
00:01:43.685 --> 00:01:47.381
Her student-marked feedback slips and says oestrogen.

32
00:01:47.381 --> 00:01:50.518
Her Male Repro deck says testosterone, twice.

33
00:01:50.518 --> 00:01:51.843
Write testosterone.

34
00:01:51.843 --> 00:01:55.121
Second: millions of sperm, but one egg a month.

35
00:01:55.121 --> 00:01:57.561
Third: only the sperm moves itself.

36
00:01:58.011 --> 00:01:58.679
<v Examiner>Once more.

37
00:01:58.679 --> 00:01:59.547
<v Examiner>The six rows.

38
00:02:01.997 --> 00:02:07.311
LH: in females it triggers ovulation; in males the Leydig cells make testosterone.

39
00:02:07.311 --> 00:02:11.718
FSH: follicle development, or spermatogenesis via the Sertoli cells.

40
00:02:11.718 --> 00:02:16.837
Timing: females start in fetal life and release eggs from puberty to menopause;

41
00:02:16.837 --> 00:02:18.911
males go from puberty, for life.

42
00:02:18.911 --> 00:02:22.670
Size: the egg is the largest cell, the sperm the smallest.

43
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:26.428
Meiosis: in females it stops and starts and gives one egg;

44
00:02:26.428 --> 00:02:29.409
in males it's continuous and gives four sperm.

45
00:02:29.409 --> 00:02:32.973
Mobility: the egg is carried by cilia; the sperm swims.
